      "reason_code": "SEC_EDGAR_METADATA_PUBLIC_DISCLOSURE",
      "state": "allowed",
      "note": "SEC EDGAR (wired 2026-09-19 via openclaw-bridge/mcp/sec-edgar/). SCOPE MATTERS, and this is deliberately NOT labelled public domain: EDGAR filings are authored by registrants, not by the government, so their expression can carry copyright. What this fetcher returns is METADATA ONLY -- company, ticker, CIK, form type, filing date, accession number, 8-K item codes and a resolvable URL -- i.e. facts about a mandatory public disclosure, which is why it is allowed. If the fetcher is ever extended to pull filing TEXT, this entry must be re-reviewed before that output can ship in a dataset. www.sec.gov is listed separately because matching here is exact-hostname, not subdomain."
